{"version":"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1","title":"EXIF - Tag | ꜱᴘᴀᴡɴ𝟐ᴘᴡɴ","description":"Personal CTF writeups and cybersecurity notes.","home_page_url":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/","language":"en","icon":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/apple-touch-icon.png","favicon":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/favicon.ico","authors":[{"name":"spawn2pwn","url":"https://github.com/nfl-alvis","avatar":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/images/IdaWin.png"}],"items":[{"title":"IoT Security Research","date_published":"2026-08-31T00:00:00&#43;07:00","date_modified":"2026-11-04T17:00:28&#43;07:00","id":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/posts/iot-security-research/","url":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/posts/iot-security-research/","authors":[{"name":"spawn2pwn","url":"https://github.com/nfl-alvis","avatar":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01c9af4b33ead25b072a03f8d0c5508?s=32&amp;d=mp"}],"tags":["PCAP Analysis","MQTT","RSA Shared Primes","AES-128-CBC","EXIF"],"summary":" Mira sent her research results from MIRA-NODE to INGGID-HUB. The gateway reported the transfer was successful, but the file never arrived at the receiver\u0026rsquo;s end. The only remaining artifact is penelitian.pcap . Trace the communication between the two devices, reconstruct the transmitted data, and find what is hidden within the research findings.\nTL;DR The research file was transmitted as 24 AES-128-CBC encrypted chunks over MQTT. The AES key was wrapped using INGGID-HUB\u0026rsquo;s RSA-1024 public key. Both devices (MIRA-NODE and INGGID-HUB) generated their RSA keys using a shared prime due to an outdated demo prototype configuration. Calculating gcd⁡(N1,N2)\\gcd(N_1, N_2)gcd(N1​,N2​) instantly factors both moduli, recovering INGGID-HUB\u0026rsquo;s private key. After decrypting the AES session key, reassembling the 24 chunks, and unzipping the archive, the flag was extracted from the EXIF ​​ UserComment metadata of dragonfly.jpg . 1. Network Reconnaissance (PCAP) We begin by inspecting the protocol hierarchy and conversation endpoints in penelitian.pcap using tshark :\n","content_html":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMira sent her research results from MIRA-NODE to INGGID-HUB. The gateway reported the transfer was successful, but the file never arrived at the receiver\u0026rsquo;s end. The only remaining artifact is \u003ccode\u003epenelitian.pcap\u003c/code\u003e . Trace the communication between the two devices, reconstruct the transmitted data, and find what is hidden within the research findings.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"details admonition abstract open\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"details-summary admonition-title\"\u003e\u003ci class=\"icon fa-solid fa-clipboard-list\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003c/i\u003eTL;DR\u003ci class=\"details-icon fa-solid fa-angle-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"details-content\"\u003e\n      \u003cdiv class=\"admonition-content\"\u003eThe research file was transmitted as 24 AES-128-CBC encrypted chunks over MQTT. The AES key was wrapped using INGGID-HUB\u0026rsquo;s RSA-1024 public key. Both devices (MIRA-NODE and INGGID-HUB) generated their RSA keys using a \u003cstrong\u003eshared prime\u003c/strong\u003e due to an outdated demo prototype configuration. Calculating \u003cspan class=\"katex\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-mathml\"\u003e\u003cmath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"\u003e\u003csemantics\u003e\u003cmrow\u003e\u003cmi\u003egcd\u003c/mi\u003e\u003cmo\u003e⁡\u003c/mo\u003e\u003cmo stretchy=\"false\"\u003e(\u003c/mo\u003e\u003cmsub\u003e\u003cmi\u003eN\u003c/mi\u003e\u003cmn\u003e1\u003c/mn\u003e\u003c/msub\u003e\u003cmo separator=\"true\"\u003e,\u003c/mo\u003e\u003cmsub\u003e\u003cmi\u003eN\u003c/mi\u003e\u003cmn\u003e2\u003c/mn\u003e\u003c/msub\u003e\u003cmo stretchy=\"false\"\u003e)\u003c/mo\u003e\u003c/mrow\u003e\u003cannotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"\u003e\\gcd(N_1, N_2)\u003c/annotation\u003e\u003c/semantics\u003e\u003c/math\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-base\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mop\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\"\u003eg\u003c/span\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mopen\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mord\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\"\u003eN\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"msupsub\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist-r\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mord mtight\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist-s\"\u003e​\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist-r\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mpunct\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mord\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\"\u003eN\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"msupsub\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist-r\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mord mtight\"\